From 0562b67860b1cb5810473da76c6ddb88997d7b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WhiteGiso <gianluca.sorbello@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:05:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/hls: keep the whole EXT-X-KEY METHOD value

method is an 11-byte buffer, but SAMPLE-AES-CTR, the method that CENC
playlists use (ClearKey among them), is 14 characters. ff_parse_key_value()
cuts the value to "SAMPLE-AES", hls_read_header() sets
key_type = KEY_SAMPLE_AES and then tries to download the key URI found in
the tag. With a data: URI the extension check rejects it, with an https URI
the request may fail as well, and in both cases the whole stream does not
open ("Unable to open key file") even when the segments are already
decrypted through the fMP4 keys passed to the segment demuxer with
seg_format_options.

Enlarge the buffer so the comparison sees the real value. SAMPLE-AES-CTR
then matches none of the methods the HLS demuxer handles and stays
KEY_NONE, exactly like a playlist without an EXT-X-KEY tag.
---
 libavformat/hls.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 2f7142f..c94288c 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@ static void handle_variant_args(struct variant_info *info, const char *key,
 
 struct key_info {
      char uri[MAX_URL_SIZE];
-     char method[11];
+     char method[16];
      char iv[35];
 };
 
